# arcode settings template.
#
# Easiest: run `arcode setup` (or ./install.sh), which writes ~/.arcode/.env for you.
# To do it by hand, copy this file to ~/.arcode/.env (your home folder), NOT to this repo:
#   mkdir -p ~/.arcode && cp .env.example ~/.arcode/.env && chmod 600 ~/.arcode/.env
# then edit ~/.arcode/.env. arcode never reads a .env inside a repo (see README > Setup).
# Variables already set in your shell override this file.

# Required: your API key. The names say ARC, but any OpenAI-compatible provider works:
# set ARC_BASE_URL below to its endpoint and put that provider's key here.
# VT ARC keys: https://llm.arc.vt.edu > profile > Settings > Account > API keys.
# (VTARC_API_KEY is accepted as an alternative name.)
ARC_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# Optional: a different OpenAI-compatible endpoint (default: VT ARC), e.g.
#   https://api.openai.com/v1  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1  http://localhost:8000/v1 (vLLM)
# ARC_BASE_URL=https://llm-api.arc.vt.edu/api/v1

# Optional: default model (otherwise arcode shows a picker; Ctrl+O changes it later).
# ARCODE_MODEL=DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash

# Optional: web search for the agent (pick one).
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:8080
